uTerm: tell the host when the frame holding a smooth scroll reaches the layer
(libghostty-spm patch 0024)

Drop this file into libghostty-spm's Patches/ghostty/ (after upstream's 0022 and
our 0023); build.sh applies it with `git apply` on every target. It is cut
against libghostty-spm 2.2.2026111701 with 0001-0023 applied, Ghostty
5ebe501a. It only adds text next to upstream's own lines: nothing inside what
0015 / 0022 insert is touched, so their anchored edits still find themselves
when the stack runs again over a patched tree.

What it does (UTERM-PATCHES.md, "滚动那一帧交到图层的信号"):
  - Surface.smoothScrollByTracked: smoothScrollBy, and numbers the scroll
    (renderer.State.scroll_seq, written in the same critical section as the
    position).
  - generic renderer: updateFrame reads the number with the position; the frame
    carries it to its completion callback (Metal Frame); after presenting, the
    callback records it (scroll_presented, atomic max).
  - Surface.smoothScrollPresented: scroll_presented >= the last number.
    Lock-free.
  - C API: ghostty_surface_smooth_scroll_by_tracked,
    ghostty_surface_smooth_scroll_presented.

Why: on iOS the scroll view's per-frame callback moves the viewport on the main
thread, the render thread draws it and queues the present on the main queue. The
callback has returned by then, so the frame is committed one refresh after the
scroll view's own (34.0 ms from the callback to glass on an iPhone at 120 Hz,
against 25.7 ms for UIKit content). A host that waits for
smoothScrollPresented before returning gets the present queued behind its
callback in the same run loop turn, and the same commit: 25.7 ms.

